   "source": [
    "# 1. OOP Fundamentals — Complete Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1.1 What is OOP?\n",
    "\n",
    "**OOP = Object-Oriented Programming**\n",
    "\n",
    "It is a programming approach where we organize a program around **objects** rather than only functions and procedures.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Basic idea\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Class → Blueprint\n",
    "Object → Real instance created from blueprint\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Car {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string color;\n",
    "    void drive() {\n",
    "        cout << \"Car is driving\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "int main() {\n",
    "    Car c1;       // Object\n",
    "    c1.color = \"Red\";\n",
    "    c1.drive();\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Car        → Class\n",
    "c1         → Object\n",
    "color      → Data Member\n",
    "drive()    → Member Function\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.2 Why OOP?\n",
    "\n",
    "Without OOP, a large program can become difficult to organize.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Procedural approach\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "string name1;\n",
    "int age1;\n",
    "\n",
    "string name2;\n",
    "int age2;\n",
    "\n",
    "void display(string name, int age) {\n",
    "    cout << name << \" \" << age;\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Data and functions are separate.\n",
    "\n",
    "### OOP approach\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << name << \" \" << age;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Now:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Student\n",
    " ├── name\n",
    " ├── age\n",
    " └── display()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The data and operations related to that data are grouped together.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.3 Procedural Programming vs OOP\n",
    "\n",
    "| Procedural                                | OOP                                                 |\n",
    "| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n",
    "| Focuses on functions                      | Focuses on objects                                  |\n",
    "| Data and functions are generally separate | Data + functions are grouped                        |\n",
    "| Less suitable for very large systems      | Better for large systems                            |\n",
    "| Reusability mainly through functions      | Reusability through classes/inheritance/composition |\n",
    "| Data protection is weaker by default      | Encapsulation provides data hiding                  |\n",
    "| Example: C                                | Example: C++                                        |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Simple mental model\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Procedural:\n",
    "\n",
    "Data ──────→ Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "OOP:\n",
    "\n",
    "Object\n",
    " ├── Data\n",
    " └── Functions\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.4 Class\n",
    "\n",
    "A **class is a blueprint/template for creating objects**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void study() {\n",
    "        cout << \"Student is studying\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The class itself describes what a `Student` should contain.\n",
    "\n",
    "It does **not automatically mean you have created a Student object**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Class Student\n",
    "     │\n",
    "     ├── name\n",
    "     ├── age\n",
    "     └── study()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.5 Object\n",
    "\n",
    "An **object is an instance of a class**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Student s1;\n",
    "Student s2;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Student → Class\n",
    "s1      → Object\n",
    "s2      → Object\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Each object has its own non-static data.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "s1.name = \"Sahil\";\n",
    "s1.age = 20;\n",
    "\n",
    "s2.name = \"Rahul\";\n",
    "s2.age = 21;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Conceptually:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "s1\n",
    "├── name = Sahil\n",
    "└── age = 20\n",
    "\n",
    "s2\n",
    "├── name = Rahul\n",
    "└── age = 21\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Both follow the same class structure but contain different data.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.6 Class vs Object\n",
    "\n",
    "### Class\n",
    "\n",
    "A class defines the structure/behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Car {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string color;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void drive() {\n",
    "        cout << \"Driving\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Object\n",
    "\n",
    "An object is created from the class.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Car car1;\n",
    "Car car2;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Think:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Class = Blueprint\n",
    "Object = Building made using blueprint\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.7 Data Members\n",
    "\n",
    "Variables declared inside a class are called **data members**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "    float marks;\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "name  → Data Member\n",
    "age   → Data Member\n",
    "marks → Data Member\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "They represent the **state/data** of an object.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Student s;\n",
    "\n",
    "s.name = \"Sahil\";\n",
    "s.age = 20;\n",
    "s.marks = 85.5;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.8 Member Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "Functions declared inside a class are called **member functions**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void study() {\n",
    "        cout << name << \" is studying\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "`study()` is a member function.\n",
    "\n",
    "It represents an **operation/behavior** of the object.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Student\n",
    "│\n",
    "├── Data\n",
    "│   └── name\n",
    "│\n",
    "└── Behavior\n",
    "    └── study()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.9 Accessing Members\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the **dot (`.`) operator** with an object.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << name;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "int main() {\n",
    "\n",
    "    Student s;\n",
    "\n",
    "    s.name = \"Sahil\";\n",
    "    s.display();\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "s.name\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Access object's name\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "s.display()\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Call object's function\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.10 Multiple Objects\n",
    "\n",
    "You can create multiple objects from one class.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Car {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string color;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << color << endl;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "int main() {\n",
    "\n",
    "    Car c1;\n",
    "    Car c2;\n",
    "    Car c3;\n",
    "\n",
    "    c1.color = \"Red\";\n",
    "    c2.color = \"Blue\";\n",
    "    c3.color = \"Black\";\n",
    "\n",
    "    c1.display();\n",
    "    c2.display();\n",
    "    c3.display();\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Conceptually:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "                 Car class\n",
    "                    │\n",
    "          ┌─────────┼─────────┐\n",
    "          ↓         ↓         ↓\n",
    "         c1        c2        c3\n",
    "       Red       Blue      Black\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Each object has its own `color`.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.11 Object Memory — Basic Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "This is important.\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "    int marks;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << age;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Student s1;\n",
    "Student s2;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Conceptually:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "s1\n",
    "┌─────────────┐\n",
    "│ age         │\n",
    "│ marks       │\n",
    "└─────────────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "s2\n",
    "┌─────────────┐\n",
    "│ age         │\n",
    "│ marks       │\n",
    "└─────────────┘\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Each object gets its own **non-static data members**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Member functions are associated with the class rather than storing a separate normal copy of the function for every object.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Important\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Student s1;\n",
    "Student s2;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "does **not** mean:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "s1 gets a completely separate copy of display()\n",
    "s2 gets a completely separate copy of display()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of the function as belonging to the class, while each object has its own state.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.12 `this` Pointer — Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "Every non-static member function has access to a special pointer called:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "this\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "It points to the **current object**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void setAge(int age) {\n",
    "        this->age = age;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "Student s;\n",
    "s.setAge(20);\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Inside:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "this\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "points to `s`.\n",
    "\n",
    "So:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "this->age\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "means:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "current object's age\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Conceptually:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "s.setAge(20)\n",
    "\n",
    "        this\n",
    "         │\n",
    "         ↓\n",
    "       ┌───────┐\n",
    "       │ age   │\n",
    "       │  20   │\n",
    "       └───────┘\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why use `this`?\n",
    "\n",
    "Especially when parameter and data member have the same name:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "void setAge(int age) {\n",
    "    this->age = age;\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Left:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "this->age\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "= object's data member\n",
    "\n",
    "Right:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "age\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "= function parameter.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.13 The Four Main OOP Concepts\n",
    "\n",
    "After learning the fundamentals, you'll encounter the famous four pillars:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "                 OOP\n",
    "                  │\n",
    "       ┌──────────┼──────────┐\n",
    "       ↓          ↓          ↓\n",
    "Encapsulation Abstraction Inheritance\n",
    "                  │\n",
    "                  ↓\n",
    "             Polymorphism\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Encapsulation\n",
    "\n",
    "Bundle data + functions together and control access.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class BankAccount {\n",
    "private:\n",
    "    int balance;\n",
    "\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    void deposit(int amount) {\n",
    "        balance += amount;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Abstraction\n",
    "\n",
    "Show necessary details while hiding unnecessary implementation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "car.start();\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "You don't need to know every internal operation of the engine.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Inheritance\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a new class using an existing class.\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Animal {\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "class Dog : public Animal {\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Animal\n",
    "   ↑\n",
    "  Dog\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4. Polymorphism\n",
    "\n",
    "One interface/name can behave differently in different situations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Animal {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    virtual void sound() {\n",
    "        cout << \"Animal sound\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "class Dog : public Animal {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    void sound() override {\n",
    "        cout << \"Bark\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.14 Complete Fundamental Example\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "#include <iostream>\n",
    "using namespace std;\n",
    "\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << \"Name: \" << name << endl;\n",
    "        cout << \"Age: \" << age << endl;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    void setAge(int age) {\n",
    "        this->age = age;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "int main() {\n",
    "\n",
    "    Student s1;\n",
    "\n",
    "    s1.name = \"Sahil\";\n",
    "    s1.setAge(20);\n",
    "\n",
    "    s1.display();\n",
    "\n",
    "    return 0;\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Flow\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Program starts\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Student class exists\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Student s1\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Object s1 created\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "s1.name = \"Sahil\"\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "s1.setAge(20)\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "this points to s1\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "s1.age becomes 20\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "s1.display()\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Print data\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.15 Terms You Must Know\n",
    "\n",
    "| Term            | Meaning                                 |\n",
    "| --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n",
    "| OOP             | Object-Oriented Programming             |\n",
    "| Class           | Blueprint/template                      |\n",
    "| Object          | Instance of a class                     |\n",
    "| Data Member     | Variable inside class                   |\n",
    "| Member Function | Function inside class                   |\n",
    "| State           | Data/value of an object                 |\n",
    "| Behavior        | Operations an object can perform        |\n",
    "| `this`          | Pointer to current object               |\n",
    "| Encapsulation   | Bundling + controlled access            |\n",
    "| Abstraction     | Hiding unnecessary implementation       |\n",
    "| Inheritance     | Creating class from another class       |\n",
    "| Polymorphism    | Same interface/name, different behavior |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🎯 What you should be able to do after Topic 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Before moving to **Topic 2: Classes & Objects**, you should be able to write these without looking:\n",
    "\n",
    "```cpp\n",
    "class Student {\n",
    "public:\n",
    "    string name;\n",
    "    int age;\n",
    "\n",
    "    void display() {\n",
    "        cout << name << \" \" << age;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "int main() {\n",
    "\n",
    "    Student s1;\n",
    "    Student s2;\n",
    "\n",
    "    s1.name = \"A\";\n",
    "    s1.age = 20;\n",
    "\n",
    "    s2.name = \"B\";\n",
    "    s2.age = 21;\n",
    "\n",
    "    s1.display();\n",
    "    s2.display();\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "And explain:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Student     → class\n",
    "s1, s2      → objects\n",
    "name, age   → data members\n",
    "display()   → member function\n",
    "this        → current object's pointer\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next logical topic: 2. Classes & Objects — including object creation, access, memory, static members, const objects, and practical exercises.**\n"
   ]
